Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0,"per_horizon":false}

Thought: The weighted hint suggests error‑based weighting; try a forward‑selection weight on a stable subset to reduce variance from only 3 windows.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool3","max_steps":10,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The weighted hint suggests error‑based weighting on a stable, small pool. Pool1 contains the top 5 models with moderate stability; applying inverse‑error weights should improve over the current best weighted w4 on full pool.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool1","metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The current leader uses a meta‑model weight (w1) which may overfit the few validation windows. A simple inverse‑error weighting with moderate shrinkage on the full pool should reduce variance while still exploiting model quality.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5,"per_horizon":false}

Thought: The current leader uses inverse-error weights on the full pool, but the ranking is only moderately stable and the error correlation is high. A meta-model based weighting might capture cross-model relationships better and reduce overfitting to the few validation windows.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w3","rationale":"use meta-model weights to improve stability"}

Thought: Remove redundant models to reduce correlated error, then weight by inverse error on the pruned pool to exploit the weighted hint.  
Action: prune_redundant  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool_full","corr_threshold":0.95,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The series is trend-dominated with moderate seasonality and the ranking is only moderately stable. A weighted combination that adapts to the trend direction may capture the downward drift better than static inverse-error weights. I will try a trend‑aware weighting on the pruned pool (pool4).  
Action: weights_error_trend  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"mae","eta":1.0}

Thought: Test the error-trend weighted combination (w8) on the full pool to see if it beats the current leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w8","rationale":"error-trend weights on reduced pool"}

Thought: The best weighted strategy uses a global meta‑model. A simple inverse‑error weighting on the pruned pool (pool4) may give a tighter, more stable combination.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The current best weighted strategy uses raw inverse-error weights on pool4. Adding shrinkage may reduce variance and improve performance.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool4","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5,"per_horizon":false}

Thought: Test the highly concentrated inverse‑error weights (w11) on the reduced pool to see if the extra shrinkage improves the already strong weighted baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w11","rationale":"highly concentrated inverse‑error weights on pool4"}

Thought: The best validation candidate is a10 (weighted w1).  
Action: accept  
Action Input: {}

